config BR2_PACKAGE_TICWATCH_PRO3_FIRMWARE
	bool "ticwatch-pro3-firmware [TicWatch Pro 3]"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE
	select BR2_PACKAGE_LINUX_FIRMWARE_BRCM_BCM43XXX
	help
	  Wi-Fi and Bluetooth firmware plumbing for the Broadcom
	  BCM43430A1 in the TicWatch Pro 3.

	  Two halves, because they come from different places:

	  The chip firmware itself is redistributable and comes from
	  linux-firmware. Upstream ships it as cypress/cyfmac43430-sdio.bin
	  with brcm/brcmfmac43430-sdio.bin as a symlink; Buildroot installs
	  the real file but not the symlink, so this package adds it.

	  The calibration data does not come from linux-firmware. The Wi-Fi
	  NVRAM and the Bluetooth patch RAM image are specific to the board
	  — in the NVRAM's case, to the individual watch, since it carries
	  the MAC address — and live on the stock Android partitions. They
	  cannot be shipped here. ticwatch-bringup finds them at boot
	  on the read-only /mnt/vendor and /mnt/persist mounts and presents
	  them under the names brcmfmac and hci_bcm ask for.

	  Without the NVRAM, brcmfmac will load and then fail to bring the
	  interface up. See the README.
